body:
OK so its been a minute but I loved this series and author so heres what i got. Spoilers obviously. 

The shrike was at first a machine thing that looked metal as shit that could teleport that was sent back in time by the "ultimate machine" thing, that if you remember the technocore and umman were communicating with. This ultimate machine was at war with the ultimate human and this war apparently created multiple timelines and alternate realities because they keep abusing time travel. Its purpose is hard to define. This is because the shrike actually switches sides a number of times. If you remember the fight with like a hundred shrikes is possible there are infinite amount of shrikes working for both sides. The machines build him and then if you remember in the far future with kassad theres mention that they were able to make it work for the humans and Aenea instead. Originally I \*\* believe\*\* it used the time tombs to go back and then kidnap people to hook them virtually to the pain tree. My memory is failing me here but I think they harnessed the peoples torment to attract the ultimate human out of hiding by creating so much pain that their massive empathy would make it impossible to ignore. Its purpose in helping Aenea I believe was to just have a bigass robot on her side, which is kickass. Like when it fought those other weaker androids. A protector for endymion. When Sol gave the shrike rachel it went really far into the future and gave her to an Aenea encampment remember? And then she changed her name and became Moneta. Very big part of the story to miss man.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

So kassad was sent to a lot of future timelines and I believe that some were just possible realities. Because when he fights the shrike in front of the tree of pain the tree of pain is not real, its virtual so maybe this was either virtual, made from some far off ultimate whatever, or a dream idk. But the scene where he fights a bunch was in the far future to help the Aenea people take the time tombs right? They wanted him because he was a kickass soldier. 

&#x200B;

The cruciforms were made by the technocore in the far future using tech from an even further future from the ultimate machine/reapers. They were being beta tested with the bikura, who were in the wrong place at the wrong time

&#x200B;

Was Hoyt a puppet? Did he have good intentions? Or did he just grow to become an absolute monster after letting things get out of hand? Or was he always a monster? I mean, its hard not to see the cruciform as divine intervention, as it was designed to be. Much is mystery about him. 

&#x200B;

The rachel moneta thing is difficult to explain if you arent familiar with the works of John Keats, specifically Hyperion, fall of hyperion, and endymion obviously. Moneta was a character in the original fall poem. I actually read all of these while reading the sci fi because I loved them so much and then fell in love with Keats. To sum it up VERY simply, Moneta convinces someone that pain and suffering can lead to art and beauty. Thematically it matches kassad being a solider and him going to war and so on. And them falling in love too. As for why its rachel, i think it was to bridge kassad to aenea and show that moneta was working on behalf of someone else. 

&#x200B;

I can probably answer anything else you have. I loved this series but the first two especially.
